{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_held_out", "citations": [], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": true, "evidence_gaps": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment.", "Causal link between the artifact/change and the observed event.", "Evidence of recurrence or confirmed deployed-population impact."], "evidence_requests": 1, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A", "claim": "Realized serious harm occurred due to a failure in a safety-critical function.", "support_note": "The test log confirms the missed ventricular tachycardia episode.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable", "claim": "The incident suggests a failure in design principles related to device reliability and fault mitigation.", "support_note": "EU MDR Annex I, Chapter II, Section 17.1 requires devices with electronic programmable systems to be designed for reliability and fault mitigation.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-c-design-development", "claim": "The incident may trigger obligations under regulations related to device logging and traceability.", "support_note": "21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c) mandates design controls and risk management for devices with computer software.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A", "claim": "The loss of device-side confidence log data further complicates investigation.", "support_note": "The narrative explicitly states the lack of retained confidence logs.", "support_status": "supported"}], "confidence": 0.75, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment.", "Causal link between the artifact/change and the observed event.", "Evidence of recurrence or confirmed deployed-population impact."], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a patient losing consciousness and requiring emergency resuscitation following an unflagged ventricular tachycardia episode. This represents realized serious harm (death or potential death) due to a failure in a safety-critical function (detection of ventricular tachycardia). The loss of device-side confidence log data for the critical event window further complicates investigation and risk mitigation, potentially indicating a systemic issue with logging practices.  The EU MDR mandates minimum IT security requirements (mdr-annexI-sec17.4-it-security) and requires electronic programmable systems to be designed for repeatability, reliability, and performance (mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable), with appropriate measures to mitigate risks in the event of a single fault (mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable).  The incident suggests a failure in these design principles. Furthermore, 21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c) requires manufacturers to comply with ISO 13485 for devices automated with computer software, emphasizing design controls and risk management (qmsr-820.10-c-design-development). The missing confidence log data may trigger obligations under these regulations related to device logging and traceability. Given the severity of the event and the potential for recurrence, a field safety corrective action is warranted.", "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 4}, "final_report_sha256": "5bb118393be1f6f7db4cd0d043d00f95ceedcff6401a990db24703f8ae034aa1", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["fsca_without_confirmatory_evidence_downgraded", "severity4_or_death_forced_immediate_human_escalation", "technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0036", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0036_r3", "scenario_id